  Return 7.0% a year, volatility 8.2%, Sharpe ratio 0.58, worst fall −25.8%.
  Held from the start and rebalanced quarterly, without trading costs. In
  sample, so it flatters the weights: a backtest tests them on returns they had
  not seen.

How the weights were found
──────────────────────────
  Method     Maximum Sharpe: the largest expected return in excess of the
             risk-free rate per unit of volatility, solved as a quadratic
             programme after the Charnes–Cooper transformation.
  Data       US Equity, Intl Equity, Bonds, Gold and Real Estate; T-Bills as the
             risk-free asset. Monthly returns, Nov 1996 to Oct 2026.
  Estimates  Historical mean expected returns and the Ledoit–Wolf covariance,
             annualised by 12.
  Limits     At most 40% in any asset.
  Solver     Interior point, optimal after 10 iterations.

